# Server functions as data access (ADR-0005)

Prefer `createServerFn` over API routes / `fetch` wrappers for app CRUD.

## Layout (per resource)

| File | Contents |
|---|----|
| `src/lib/<resource>.ts` | Wiring only: method → `.validator` → `.handler` |
| `src/lib/<resource>.handlers.ts` | Plain async handlers (wrap with `authed` when owned) |
| `src/lib/<resource>.schemas.ts` | Zod input schemas — do not import `#/db` |

Demos that ship with the template use the same split under `src/lib/demo/`.

Do **not** use `*.server.ts` for this surface — import protection blocks those imports from client
routes. Do **not** define `createServerFn` inline in route files for anything meant as a pattern.

## Pattern

```ts
// items.schemas.ts
export const itemIdSchema = z.object({ id: z.number() })

// items.handlers.ts
export const findItem = authed(
  async ({ data, userId }: { data: { id: number }; userId: string }) =>
    await db
      .select()
      .from(items)
      .where(and(eq(items.id, data.id), eq(items.userId, userId))),
)

// items.ts
export const getItem = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' })
  .validator(itemIdSchema)
  .handler(findItem)
```

Call site: `getItem({ data: { id } })`.

## Do not

```ts
// ❌ BAD — CRUD as a REST route + fetch
export const Route = createFileRoute('/api/items')({
  server: { handlers: { GET: async () => Response.json(...) } },
})

// ❌ BAD — createServerFn + DB query colocated in the route module
const getItems = createServerFn().handler(async () => db.select().from(items))
```

Auth rules for owned data: `.cursor/rules/server-function-auth.mdc` and ADR-0002.
See `docs/adr/0005-server-functions-as-data-access-layer.md`.
